<div class="card mt-4 p-5">
  <p class="eyebrow">Optional: uploads, forum posts and comments</p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">Tick the User permission when you create the key, and Sherlock also tracks how many torrents you uploaded, your forum posts and your torrent comments.</p>
  <p class="hint mt-2">
    Redacted's User permission also gives access to your private messages, and there's no way to allow one without the other.
    Sherlock never reads, stores or sends messages. If you'd rather not trust that, run Sherlock yourself.
    <%= link_to "Get the source code", Rails.configuration.x.source_url, class: "link", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>
    <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right text-xs"></i>
  </p>
</div>
